cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Code for: Free-streaming neutrinos leave a step in the primordial black hole mass function"
authors:
  - family-names: McCormick
    given-names: Stephen
    affiliation: "Division of Mathematical Sciences, Luleå University of Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/quasilocal/PBH_neutrino_simulation"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Simulation code, stored results and scripts for the paper "Free-streaming
  neutrinos leave a step in the primordial black hole mass function". The code
  follows the general-relativistic collapse of spherical perturbations with the
  photon-electron plasma as a fluid and the neutrinos by their transport
  equation, coupled by collision terms that decouple them at a physical rate,
  and reproduces the thresholds, figures and tables of the paper
  (python reproduce.py). The code was generated by the AI system Claude Opus 5.5
  (Anthropic) under the author's direction.
keywords:
  - primordial black holes
  - neutrino decoupling
  - free streaming
  - numerical relativity
  - radiation transport
